From 61bee8c9ad00e1fa546350ddb872662e13776599 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Skynizz <182822215+Skynizz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:48:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] KRC as the indirect cache (pt_cache 2), first in-game version
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- World-space cells (≈ pt_krc_cell_px pixels, power-of-2 levels,
  per face), K = 4 offset cells per pixel, truncated mean.
- Neyman allocation per pixel (pt_krc_ppp × sigma / mean sigma), without a
  task list; paths from the primary surface with the game's lighting,
  resampling on mature cells.
- Correlated paths: each sample evaluates the direct light with the
  intensity of the animated lamps in the frame and in the previous one
  (the game's prev_style_scale); the difference corrects the history.
- Detection of unexplained changes (doors, objects).
- Reading: the pixel's diffuse indirect comes from the cells, with no ray;
  the specular reflection stays the game's.
- English compiler (VSLANG): Ninja finally follows the headers.

---
